      "content": "The idea of \"rebuilding\" is a massive, exhausting concept when you're already feeling hollowed out. You're right, you can't erase the past, but you can choose what you do with the present moment, even if it's just a tiny breath. If the future feels like a pointless performance, perhaps the only honest thing to do is to stop performing altogether. Just let yourself be still, and let the pressure to \"be something\" finally lift.",
